<h2> Plot story</h2>
<p> Gregor Samsa awakens one morning transformed into a monstrous insect. Initially viewing the change as temporary, he worries about missing work as a traveling salesman, a job he despises but retains to pay off his father’s debts. 

When his chief clerk visits to inform him that the country has announced it is going to impose a lockdown because of a mysterious virus, Gregor unlocks the door. Horrified by his appearance, the clerk flees, and his father angrily forces Gregor back into his room,
    
injuring him in the process. The family kept Gregor locked away. His sister, Grete, becomes his primary caregiver, feeding him with her food and removing furniture so he can crawl freely on the walls. However, Gregor began to see her with different eyes, loving eyes,
    
but he didn't want to follow the same pattern as in Monterrey; he always thought marrying your sister was disgusting, but now it didn't seem like a bad idea. In the end, they still loved each other. 

Over time, the pandemic was coming to an end. Gregor's family remade their lives without him; they kept him locked away, but one day, Gregor had a plan: he was going to confess his love. He finally felt confident and sure to ask her out. 

One evening, he escaped from the room they had him locked in, sneaked into the living room, and there she was, as beautiful as always, with those eyes and her big heart. Drawn by Grete’s violin music, finally, after all these years, he was going to do it;

he tried to get her attention, but suddenly, everything went black, and in an instant, he could no longer move. She walked, didn't see him or hear him; she had stepped on him, yet he felt neither anger nor sadness; 

he was happy that this had been the first and final physical contact between them. Grete took care of him all those years, but she didn't even notice he was gone forever.  

